$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.2. Preparation of ethyl
2-((Z)-5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)-2,4-dioxothiazolidin-3-yl)acetates
(4a-h) Typical procedure: A mixture of
1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-carboxaldehyde 1a (0.5 g, 2 mmol) and ethyl
2-(2,4-dioxothiazolidin-3-yl)acetate 3 (0.4 g, 2 mmol) in ethanol (20 mL)
and 2-3 drops of piperidine was refluxed for 4-5 h. A solid was separated
out of the reaction mixture within 15-20 min and the refluxing was
continued for 4-5 h to complete the reaction. The reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature, filtered, and washed with ethanol to give the
pure product 4a. The other derivatives 4b-h were synthesized by adopting
the similar procedure. 4.4. Ethyl
2-((Z)-2,4-dioxo-5-((1-phenyl-3-p-tolyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidin-3-yl)acetate
(4b), yield 92%. IR (νmax, KBr) cm-1: 1736, 1690, 1605, 1520, 1450, 1373,
1311, 1219, 1142, 1095, 1026. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 400 MHz, δ): 8.812 (s, 1H,
Pyrazolyl H), 8.041-8.022 (m, 2H, Ar H), 7.739 (s, 1H, =CH) 7.598-7.536
(m, 4H, Ar H), 7.448-7.379 (m, 3H, Ar H), 4.480 (s, 2H, NCH2),
4.199-4.145 (q, 2H, -OCH2CH3), 2.405 (s, 3H, Ph CH3), 1.231-1.195 (t, 3H,
-OCH2CH3). MS (ESI+) m/z 448 [M+H]. Anal. Found: C, 64.0; H, 4.98; N,
9.2. C24H21N3O4S requires C, 64.41; H, 4.73, N, 9.39%. Melting points
(°C): 225-227.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Knoevenagel condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of new pyrazolyl-2,4-thiazolidinediones as antibacterial and
antifungal agents
