$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
(Z)-5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-diones
(3a–h) A mixture of 1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-carboxaldehyde (1a, 1g, 4
mmol) and thiazolidine-2,4-dione (2, 0.51 g, 5 mmol) in ethanol (20 ml)
and 2–3 drops of piperidine, was refluxed. A solid separated out of the
reaction mixture within 15–20 min and the refluxing was continued for 5–6
h to complete the reaction. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, filtered and washed with ethanol to give the pure product.
(Z)-5-((3-(4-fluorophenyl)-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-dione
(3e), 92% IR cm-1 (KBr): 1759 (C=O, thiazolidinedione ring), 1697 (C=O,
thiazolidinedione ring), 1589, 1520, 1443, 1404, 1327, 1234, 1149, 1065
and 1003; 1H NMR δ (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): 12.8–12.7 (bs, 1H, NH, exch. D2O),
8.653 (s, 1H, Pyrazolyl-H), 7.999–7.972 (d, 2H, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.770–7.744
(d, 2H, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.598–7.496 (m, 5H), 7.431–7.382 (m, 1H). 13C NMR δ
(75 MHz, DMSO-d6): 168.22, 168.11, 154.00, 139.31, 131.44, 131.33,
130.19, 128.62, 128.42, 127.88, 122.02, 119.78, 116.78, 116.55 and
116.36; Anal. Found: C, 62.34; H, 3.52; N, 11.6. C19H12FN3O2S (365.38)
requires C, 62.46; H, 3.31; N, 11.50%. Mp = 298–300 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Knoevenagel condensation
