$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):AMD
$DATUM surface reaction products with SBA-15
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of Rhodanines (3a-3g) and
2,4-Thiazolidinediones (3h-3n) . A mixture of the aromatic aldehyde (1
mmol), 2,4-thiazolidinedione (0.133, 1 mmol) [or rhoda-nine (0.117 g, 1
mmol)] and SBA-15-Pr-NH2 (0.05 g) in EtOH (5 mL) was stirred at 50°C in
an oil bath for 2 hours; the progress of the reaction was monitored by
TLC (2:1 n-hexane/ethyl acetate). After completion of the reaction, 10 mL
acetone was added and the mixture was filtered to remove the catalyst.
Upon addition of 5 mL H2O to the filtrate, the precipitated solid
obtained was collected and recrystallized from ethanol. The pure
products, characterized by comparison of their 1H NMR spectra and melting
points with those reported in the literature. Compound: 3a. Mp: Found:
202-204 °C; Lit.: 199-2024 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, solid-supported catalyst, catalyst prepared and
used, recyclable catalyst, silica support used, Knoevenagel condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 5-Alkylidene-2,4-thiazolidinediones and Rhodanines Promoted
by Propylamino-functionalized Nano-structured SBA-15
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Veisi, Hojat; Naeimi, Alireza; Maleki, Behrooz; Ashrafi, Samaneh Sedigh;
Sedrpoushan, Alireza
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2015), 47(4), 309-315

