$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of 2-styrylbenzimidazoles 6(a-x)
from 2-methylbenzimidazole 5(a-c). An intimate mixture of 5(a-c) (1.32 g,
10 mmol), aromatic aldehyde 1(a-h) (10 mmol) and boric acid (10 mol%) was
dissolved in 10 ml of glycerol in a 250-ml round bottom flask and allowed
to boil at 160-180 °C for 5-6 h. At the end of this period, the reaction
mixture was poured into ice cold water (25 ml). The reaction mixture was
diluted with ethylacetate, and the organic layer was separated, dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4. The product was obtained after removal of the
solvent under reduced pressure and recrystallized from ethanol. 6 (a-x).
The structures of the products were confirmed by IR, 1H NMR, mass
spectral data, and comparison with authentic samples. S. no.: 8. Product:
6h; Yield: 90%. (E)-2-(2-(Thiophen-2-yl)vinyl)-1H-benzimidazole (6h).
Light green crystals. M.p 198-200 °C, IR (KBr, ν max in cm-1): 3405
(-NH), 3101 (=C-H), 1894 (C=N), 1633 (C=C), 1H NMR (DMSO-d6 , 400 MHz) δ
ppm: 6.93 (d, 1H, -C=CH (vinylic proton), J H-H = 16.4 Hz),7.17 (t, 1H,
thiophenyl proton), 7.25 (q, 2H, phenylic protons), 7.44 (d, 1H,
thiophenyl proton), 7.59 (q, 2H, phenylic protons), 7.67 (d, 1H,
thiophenyl proton), 7.94 (d, 1H, -CH=C-(vinylic proton), J H-H = 16.4
Hz), 10.0 (s, 1H, -NH of benzimidazole), 13C NMR (DMSO-d6 , 100 MHz) δ
ppm: 114.47, 114.50, 122.87, 127.96, 128.51, 129.15, 129.48, 137.39,
140.33, 149.87 (6 aryl carbons (attached to imidazole ring), 4 thiophenyl
carbons, 2 vinylic carbons and 1 imidazole quaternary carbon), MS (m/z):
227.07 (M+ .), Anal. Calcd. for C13H10N2S:C, 69.00;H, 4.45;N, 12.38; S,
14.17 %Found:C, 69.24; H, 4.52; N, 12.40; S, 14.27 %.
