$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of
(Z)-5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-diones
(3a–h) A mixture of 1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-carboxaldehyde (1a, 1g, 4
mmol) and thiazolidine-2,4-dione (2, 0.51 g, 5 mmol) in ethanol (20 ml)
and 2–3 drops of piperidine, was refluxed. A solid separated out of the
reaction mixture within 15–20 min and the refluxing was continued for 5–6
h to complete the reaction. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, filtered and washed with ethanol to give the pure product.
3a (1.25 g, 90% yield) IR cm-1 (KBr): 1736 (C=O, thiazolidinedione ring),
1690 (C=O, thiazolidinedione ring), 1605, 1528, 1504, 1443, 1412, 1366,
1327, 1234, 1149, 1065 and 1026; 1H NMR δ (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): 12.6–12.4
(bs, 1H, NH, exch. D2O), 8.664 (s, 1H, Pyrazolyl-H), 8.015–7.989 (m, 2H),
7.681–7.623 (m, 2H), 7.584–7.491 (m, 6H), 7.430–7.380 (m, 1H); 13C NMR δ
(75 MHz, DMSO-d6): 168.95, 168.61, 153.93, 139.27, 131.90, 130.09,
129.40, 129.13, 128.33, 127.89, 124.41, 121.57, 119.80 and 116.25; Anal.
Found: C, 65.5; H, 3.66; N, 11.9. C19H13N3O2S (347.39) requires C, 65.69;
H, 3.77; N, 12.10%. Mp = 292–294 °C, Lit. Mp = 263–265 °C (Youssef et
al., 2010)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Knoevenagel condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and antimicrobial activity of
5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-diones
