$DATUM surface reaction products with SBA-15
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
2-Amino-5-alkylidenethiazol-4-ones (4a-4h) . A mixture of rhodanine
(0.117 g, 1 mmol), ketone (1 mmol), amine (1 mmol), and SBA-15-Pr-NH2
(0.05 g) in aqueous ethanol (1:1, 4 mL) was stirred under reflux for 2
hours; the progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC (2:1
n-hexane/ethyl acetate). After completion of the reaction, 10 mL acetone
was added and the mixture was filtered to remove the catalyst. Addition
of 5 mL H2O to the filtrate gave a solid which was collected and
recrystallized from ethanol (80%) or purified by column chromatography.
The pure product. All the products are known and were characterized by
comparison of their 1H NMR and melting point data with those reported in
the literature. Compound: 4e; Yield: 90%. Mp: Found: 141-143°C; Lit.:
140-14215 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, solid-supported catalyst, catalyst prepared and
used, recyclable catalyst, silica support used, Knoevenagel condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 5-Alkylidene-2,4-thiazolidinediones and Rhodanines Promoted
by Propylamino-functionalized Nano-structured SBA-15
