$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
Knoevenagel adducts pyrazolonylidenemethylquinolones 5a-h. N-Allyl
quinolone 3a-b (1.12 mmol), pyrazolone 4a-d (1.12 mmol, 1 eq.) and TBA-HS
(20 mol %) were well mixed in a round-bottom flask and heated to 100 °C
for 20-35 min with constant stirring. After completion of the reaction as
confirmed by TLC (ethyl acetate/n-hexane 3:7), reaction mass was cooled
to room temperature, solid residue was obtained, which was crystallized
from methanol.
1-Allyl-7-chloro-3-{(Z)-[1-(2-chlorophenyl)-3-methyl-1,5-dihydro-4H-pyrazol-5-one-4-ylidene]methyl}quinolin-2(1H)-one
5f. Orange solid, yield 89 %, 437 mg. Time: 25 min. mp 226-228 °C; Rf =
0.44 (ethyl acetate/n-hexane 3:7); IR (νmax, cm-1): 3,053, 2,916, 2,851,
1,687, 1,651, 1,587, 1,485, 1,358, 1,229, 1,159, 1,061, 995, 812, 768,
716, 681; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.40 (s, 3 H, CH3), 4.98 (d, J = 4.4
Hz, 2H, CH2), 5.17 (d, J = 17.2 Hz, 1H, one of ═CH2), 5.32 (d, J = 10.8
Hz, 1H, the other of ═CH2), 6.01 (m, 1H, CH), 7.23-7.72 (m, 7H, Ar-H),
8.21 (s, 1H, -CH═), 10.28 (s, 1H, Ar-H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): 13.59
(CH3), 44.86 (CH2), 116.12, 117.51 (═CH2), 121.41, 123.46, 123.35,
127.32, 127.64, 128.53, 130.66, 131.36, 131.84, 132.65, 133.43, 135.21,
136.76, 140.68, 141.32, 146.27, 151.47 (arom.), 161.43 (C2═O), 162.79
(C5'═O); ESI-MS: m/z: 438.1 (M+H)+, Anal Calcd for C23H17Cl2N3O2: C,
63.03; H, 3.91; N, 9.59; Found: C, 63.21; H, 4.09; N, 9.70.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, no solvent, Knoevenagel condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
