$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
(Z)-5-((3-aryl-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-diones
(3a–h) A mixture of 1,3-diphenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-carboxaldehyde (1a, 1g, 4
mmol) and thiazolidine-2,4-dione (2, 0.51 g, 5 mmol) in ethanol (20 ml)
and 2–3 drops of piperidine, was refluxed. A solid separated out of the
reaction mixture within 15–20 min and the refluxing was continued for 5–6
h to complete the reaction. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, filtered and washed with ethanol to give the pure product.
(Z)-5-((3-(4-chlorophenyl)-1-phenyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)methylene)thiazolidine-2,4-dione
(3d), 88% IR cm-1 (KBr): 1751 (C=O, thiazolidinedione ring), 1690(C=O,
thiazolidinedione ring), 1605, 1504, 1450, 1412,1335, 1227, 1142, 1095,
1057 and 1018; 1H NMR δ(300 MHz, DMSO-d6): 12.7–12.5 (bs, 1H, NH, exch.
D2O),8.694 (s, 1H, Pyrazolyl-H), 8.019–7.993 (m, 2H), 7.710–7.665 (m,
2H), 7.586–7.529 (m, 3H), 7.440–7.384 (m, 3H);13C NMR δ (75 MHz,
DMSO-d6): 168.12, 167.91, 153.00,139.21, 131.34, 131.23, 130.09, 128.51,
128.31, 127.97,122.06, 119.84, 116.58, 116.29 and 116.05; Anal. Found:
C,59.65; H, 3.36; N, 10.8. C19H12ClN3O2S (381.84) requires C, 59.76; H,
3.17; N, 11.00%. Mp = 325–327 °C, Lit. Mp = 280–282 °C (Youssef et al.,
2010)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
